%N A373534 Decimal expansion of Pi^(1/2)*Gamma(1/20)/(10*Gamma(11/20)).
%C A373534 Constants from generalized Pi integrals: the case of n=20.
%H A373534 Takayuki Tatekawa, <a href="/A373534/b373534.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10001</a>
%H A373534 <a href="/index/Tra#transcendental">Index entries for transcendental numbers</a>.
%F A373534 Equals 2*Integral_{x=0..1} dx/sqrt(1-x^20).
%F A373534 Equals (2*sqrt(Pi)*Gamma(21/20))/Gamma(11/20). - _Peter Luschny_, Jun 17 2024
%F A373534 Equals B(1/20, 1/2)/10, where B is the beta function. Hence the constant is transcendental by a theorem of Schneider (1941). - _Charles R Greathouse IV_, Jul 26 2026
%e A373534 2.135344933248004228046475279683...
%p A373534 (2*sqrt(Pi)*GAMMA(21/20))/GAMMA(11/20): evalf(%, 102); # _Peter Luschny_, Jun 17 2024
%t A373534 RealDigits[2*Sqrt[Pi]/20*Gamma[1/20]/Gamma[11/20], 10, 5001][[1]]
%o A373534 (PARI) 2*sqrt(Pi)*gamma(21/20)/gamma(11/20) \\ _Charles R Greathouse IV_, Jul 26 2026
